{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"供应链基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/ecommerce/supply-chain-management/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"supply-chain-architecture","title":"供应链网络架构与参考模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ecommerce/supply-chain-management/foundations/supply-chain-architecture","wordCount":1523,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"demand-planning-forecasting","title":"需求计划与预测方法","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ecommerce/supply-chain-management/foundations/demand-planning-forecasting","wordCount":1416,"readingTime":6},{"seq":3,"slug":"procurement-supplier-management","title":"采购与供应商管理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ecommerce/supply-chain-management/foundations/procurement-supplier-management","wordCount":1550,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"供应链基础\">供应链基础</h1><p>本章建立供应链管理的基本心智模型。从供应链的网络架构、关键参与角色讲起，深入需求计划与预测方法论，最后落到采购与供应商管理的核心实践。</p>\n<p>掌握这三篇内容后，你将拥有供应链&quot;计划-源-造&quot;（Plan-Source-Make）的完整认知框架，能够理解后续章节中物流执行、技术赋能与战略决策的底层逻辑。</p>\n<p>对于开发者而言，这些基础概念直接映射到供应链系统的核心数据模型——BOM（物料清单）、MRP（物料需求计划）、ATP（可承诺量）等模块的设计都源于此处的业务逻辑。</p>\n"}